  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Remove seeds from cukes with thumb. Toss cucumber, tomato, olive oil, red wine vinegar, red onion, and white pepper together in a large bowl; season with salt. Refrigerate until slightly chilled, 10 to 15 minutes.",
      "group": null
    }
  ],
  "footnotes": [],
  "nutrition": null,
  "importedNotes": [
    {
      "text": "I love this salad and make it all summer long. I use about half the oil, and I add a little sugar (maybe a teaspoon or two for this amount of veggies) and some chopped fresh oregano and parsley (a tablespoon or so of each--they add eye appeal, too). And I usually do a quick seeding of the tomatoes & cukes with my thumb just to help cut down on the liquid. Goes great with grilled anything!"
    }
